 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186101607 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186101942 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186101608 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186101755 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186101608 #edb/ref 1061 12339 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186101608 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "22f4b88d-3d39-5cdb-8f96-eef99b7f8d43" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186101608 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186100827 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186101609 #edb/ref 1061 12340 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186101609 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "822556de-6ecc-5575-befa-a8d021246130" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186101609 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186100828 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186101755 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186101609 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186101755 #edb/ref 1061 22970 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186101755 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "9b64bab5-b9b1-5d61-9e9d-6f44ed48f4e9" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186101755 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186100919 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186101756 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186101608 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186101756 #edb/ref 1061 22971 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186101756 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "9694c0be-fabb-57e1-9b70-9ee9fc1f9bdc" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186101756 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186100920 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186101942 #edb/ref 1064 "Let's suppose we only know the values of the functions $f(x)$ and $g(x)$ at $x=0$ along with their derivatives, as given in the table below.\n\n| $x$ | $f(x)$ | $g(x)$ | $f'(x)$ | $g'(x)$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $0$ | $2$ | $3$ | $4$ | $5$ |\n\nCan we calculate $\\dfrac{\\textrm{d}}{\\textrm{d}x}\\Big( f(x)g(x)\\Big )$ at $x=0?$\n\nUsing the product rule, we have\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{\\textrm{d}}{\\textrm{d}x}\\Big( f(x)g(x)\\Big) = f'(x)g(x)+f(x)g'(x).\n$$\n\nAt the point where $x=0,$ this gives\n\n$$\n\\left.\\dfrac{\\textrm{d}}{\\textrm{d}x}\\Big( f(x)g(x)\\Big) \\right|_{x=0}\t=\tf'(0)g(0)+f(0)g'(0).\n$$\n\nAll of these values are given in the table! So, substituting the values from the table into the formula, we conclude that\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(f(x)g(x))|}_{x=0} & ={f}^{'}(0)g(0)+f(0){g}^{'}(0) \\\\  & =4\\cdot 3+2\\cdot 5 \\\\  & =22.\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186101942 #edb/ref 1065 2627 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186101942 #edb/ref 1066 #uuid "9df0b4fa-df54-5f34-9bdc-3fc11befd2e8" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186101942 #edb/ref 1067 "Introduction" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186239021 #edb/ref 1080 "15\\pi " #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186239021 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186239021 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "6fdf7b57-fa6c-5c2c-be3a-d2a8d9526afa" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186239421 #edb/ref 1080 "-\\pi " #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186239421 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186239421 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "9d21044d-5bc1-535e-bb91-61e14957e543" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186239525 #edb/ref 1080 "-15\\pi " #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186239525 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186239525 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "a8a2dc1c-daa1-5a37-893e-e516b10c06f7" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186239800 #edb/ref 1080 "7\\pi " #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186239800 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186239800 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "c67ec0cd-471c-5a08-80b1-1299eda3cb53" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186239911 #edb/ref 1080 "15-2{\\pi }^{2}" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186239911 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186239911 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "d385678e-bb07-5f09-8884-65e846069242" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186240727 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186239021 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186240727 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186239421 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186240727 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186239525 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186240727 #edb/ref 1075 #ed